course: dictionary
lesson: 2144
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around a word are its context, and they tell you which meaning is meant.
explain: «African grey parrots are famous copiers of sounds.» Parrots do not use photocopiers, so copier here means something that copies. These parrots copy their flock's calls and the noises in the house.
explain: Now think about a school office. «The copier is jammed» means the paper machine has stopped working. A copier is a machine that makes paper copies, so the clue is the jam. Read the whole sentence before you decide which meaning fits.
fact: A copier is a machine that makes paper copies of documents and pictures.
fact: A photocopier is another name for a copier.
fact: A copier can also be a person who copies, especially someone who copies other people's work.
fact: A paper jam means paper is stuck inside a copier.
fact: African grey parrots are copiers of sounds: wild ones copy their flock's calls, and pet ones copy words and household noises.
exercise: «The copier is jammed, so we cannot print the worksheets.» What is a copier in this sentence? | A pen for writing | *A machine that makes paper copies | A person who copies other people's work | A bird that copies sounds
exercise: «Ben is a copier who looks at Sam's answers during the test.» What does copier mean here? | A machine that makes paper copies | A teacher who marks tests | A parrot that copies words | *A person who copies other people's work
exercise: Which word is another name for a copier? | printer | copper | *photocopier | crayon
test: «The copier is out of paper, so we cannot print the test.» What is the copier? | A school bag | *A machine | A parrot | A person who copies
test: Which phrase means paper is stuck inside a copier? | a paper hat | a paper plane | a paper boat | *a paper jam
exam: «African grey parrots are famous copiers of sounds.» What does copiers mean here? | *Things that copy sounds they hear | Machines that print | People who make worksheets | Teachers who mark tests
